{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe heat here is stifling, yet the mind finds its cool in the Louvre. I returned today to the gallery before the living painters take over the walls. Raumer and Panofka were there; we discussed the transition from ideal to actuality in art, though they lacked the depth to grasp the necessity of the movement. Cousin’s company earlier was pleasant enough, if somewhat superficial.\n\nIn the evening, the Théâtre-Français offered a respite. Mlle Mars in *Alzire* possesses a dignity that borders on the tragic, while Leverd in *Emilia* showed the lighter, more immediate side of feeling. It is good to see the ethical life played out on stage, even if the French conception of freedom remains bound to the particular.\n\nI am tired but content. The journey continues, but my thoughts remain with you and the boys in Berlin. Do not worry; I am eating well and keeping my spirits high.\n\nYours ever,\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795080680,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":213,"prompt_tokens":952,"total_tokens":1165,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-SkR4e3ruHkgNvdVmTqjh8TQcHshXdZTx","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":952,"prompt_ms":902.218,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9477079831932773,"prompt_per_second":1055.177351815193,"predicted_n":213,"predicted_ms":5095.167,"predicted_per_token_ms":24.033806603773588,"predicted_per_second":41.608057204013136}}